+## How Defaults Are Shown
+
+The help bracket and prompts show a default through two functions of the module `click._default_text`:
+`default_help_text(option, ctx)` is the text of the `default` item of the option's help bracket (`2` in
+`[default: 2]`), or `None` when the help shows no default, and `default_prompt_text(value, type)` is the text that a
+prompt shows between the brackets for its default value (`alice` in `Name [alice]: `).
+
+```python
+from click._default_text import default_help_text, default_prompt_text
+
+opt = click.Option(["--n"], default=2, show_default=True)
+ctx = click.Context(click.Command("cli", params=[opt]))
+assert default_help_text(opt, ctx) == "2"
+assert default_prompt_text("alice") == "alice"
+```
+
 ## Showing Environment Variables
 
 To control the appearance of environment variables pass `show_envvar`.
